hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"688","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated: Marwan used to appoint Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) as the governor of Madinah. Whenever Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a man dragging his lower garment or striking his feet on the ground, he would say: ""The matter has come,"" then he would say that Abu al-Qasim (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah does not look (with mercy) at the person who drags his lower garment out of pride."""
"689","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated: Marwan used to appoint Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) as governor over Madinah, and he narrated similar to the previous hadith."
"690","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him (with mercy)."""
"691","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear both (shoes) together or take both off together. When you put on your shoes, start with the right, and when you take them off, start with the left."""
"692","From another chain of narration, a hadith similar to the previous one is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"693","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you puts on shoes, let him start with the right, and when he takes them off, let him start with the left. Let him wear both shoes together or keep both feet bare."""
"694","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(Among the Children of Israel) there was a man who, wearing a suit and combing his hair in locks, was walking arrogantly when he was made to sink into the earth, and he will continue to sink in it until the Day of Resurrection.”"
"695","From another chain of narration, a similar hadith is reported from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) as the previous one."
"696","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man was walking."" Then he mentioned as in the previous hadith."
"697","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Among the people before you (the Children of Israel), there was a young man who, wearing a pair of garments, was walking arrogantly in pride, when the earth swallowed him up, and he will continue to sink in it until the Day of Resurrection."""
"698","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) strictly forbade (wearing) silk. A man said to Abdullah bin Shaqiq: You too are wearing silk. He replied: Subhan Allah! This is not silk. The man said: Its warp is of silk. Abdullah bin Shaqiq said: I did not know that."
"699","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (wearing) a gold ring."
"700","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A woman who practiced tattooing was brought to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: I adjure you by Allah, has any one of you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this? Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I stood up and said: O Commander of the Believers! I have heard (something) from him. He said: What have you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? I said: I heard him say: ""Do not tattoo, and do not get tattooed."" (That is, making marks on the body with a needle and filling them with color.)"
"701","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah! Are there two gold bangles? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are two bangles of fire."" She said: O Messenger of Allah! Are there two gold earrings? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are two earrings of fire."" She said: O Messenger of Allah! If a woman does not adorn herself for her husband, she will become undesirable to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who has forbidden you from making silver earrings and coloring them yellow with ambergris (compound perfume) or saffron so that they become like gold?"""
"702","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Any caravan in which there is a bell is deprived of the companionship of the angels of mercy."""
"703","Sayyida Rabi’ bint Mu’awwidh bin ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I brought a tray of fresh dates to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and small cucumbers with a slight fuzz on them were gifted to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) placed a gold ornament in my hand and said: “Wear it.”"
"704","It is narrated from Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umm Ayman! Keep your shawl/veil hidden from us."""
"705","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid al-Sakan (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a woman wearing two gold bangles, so he said to her: ""Do you like that Allah should make you wear two bangles of fire?"" So she threw them away, and after that, we did not see them on her again."
"706","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The sleeves of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were up to the wrist."
"707","Abu Salih narrated from Salman the same (hadith)."
"708","Badeel bin Maisarah Al-Uqaili narrated: The sleeves of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) were up to the wrists."
"709","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman who wears a gold necklace around her neck will have a necklace of fire put on her like it, and the woman who wears a gold earring in her ear will have an earring of fire put in her ear like it on the Day of Resurrection."""
"710","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding the hem of women’s garments: “One span.” I said: Then their shins will become exposed. He (peace be upon him) said: “Then one hand (is sufficient).”"
"711","The sister of Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (Fatimah bint al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us, and said: ""O assembly of women! Do you not have any inclination towards wearing silver for your adornment? For any woman who wears gold jewelry for the purpose of display will be punished because of it."""
"712","The sister of Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (Fatimah bint al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us; the narrator mentioned it similar to the previous hadith."
"713","Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: ""When any of you comes to pray the ‘Isha prayer, she should not apply perfume."""
"714","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man who had dyed his hair with henna, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How good this is."" Then he passed by another man who had dyed his hair with henna and katam, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is better than that."" Then he passed by another man who had dyed his hair yellow, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the best of all of them."" The narrator stated: Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) used to dye his hair yellow."
"715","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man's thigh, so he said to him: ""Cover your thigh, for the thigh of a man is part of his 'awrah (private parts)."""
